.TH VIRTICLE 1 "" "virticle" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
virticle \- web controller for KVM/libvirt hosts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B virticle
[\fIflags\fR]
.br
.B virticle version
.br
.B virticle backup
[\fB\-o\fR \fIfile|dir\fR] [\fB\-\-encrypt\fR]
.br
.B virticle restore
\fIfile\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Virticle is one program that serves a web UI and API and manages libvirt
nodes over SSH. Nothing is installed on the managed nodes. The controller
keeps its users, node list, task log and audit log in a SQLite database in
the data directory.
.PP
The package runs it as the systemd service
.B virticle.service
as user
.BR virticle ,
serving HTTPS with a self-signed certificate on port 8443. The journal says
which address to open to create the administrator account.
.SH OPTIONS
Run
.B virticle \-help
for the full list. The main flags are:
.TP
.BI \-listen " address"
Address to serve the web UI and API on. Given, it overrides the settings of
the Web access page. A non-loopback address serves HTTPS with a generated
self-signed certificate.
.TP
.BI \-data " dir"
Directory for the database and the controller's SSH key (default
/var/lib/virticle if it holds a database, else data).
.TP
.B \-no\-scheduler
Do not run scheduled snapshots and backups from this controller.
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version, commit and build date and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VIRTICLE_JUMP_PASSWORD
Password for node jump hosts.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/virticle/virticle.env
Service environment: VIRTICLE_ARGS (extra flags) and VIRTICLE_JUMP_PASSWORD.
Kept across upgrades.
.TP
.I /var/lib/virticle
Data directory: virticle.db, id_ed25519, known_hosts, instance\-id. Copies of
the database made before a schema upgrade are named
.IR virticle.db.bak\-<version>\-<time> .
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR /usr/share/doc/virticle/install.md
